<template>
    <heading>Local storage</heading>
    <keywords><li>local storage</li><li>directory handle</li><li>File System Access API</li></keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>storage.local.open(directoryHandle, root_filename = directoryHandle.name)</code> creates a project backed by the supplied directory handle. The optional root filename defaults to the directory name. The handle is retained privately and is never exposed through the returned project object.</p>
        <p>Loads and listings accept an <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal"><code>AbortSignal</code></a>. Cancellation is checked before and after local operations, but cannot interrupt native file reads. Stores and removals accept no signal: stopping the caller's wait cannot establish that a modification did not commit. Stores await <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FileSystemWritableFileStream"><code>FileSystemWritableFileStream</code></a> close and attempt abort on failure; a newly created empty file may remain if storing fails.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code"><name>Local storage backend</name><code><![CDATA[    const local = {
        open(handle, root_filename = handle?.name) {
            if (handle?.kind !== "directory") throw new Error("Expected a directory handle");
            return project(local, handle, root_filename);
        },
        async load(name, signal) {
            const directory = location(this);
            filename(name);
            signal?.throwIfAborted();
            const handle = await directory.getFileHandle(name);
            const file = await handle.getFile();
            const text = await file.text();
            signal?.throwIfAborted();
            return text;
        },
        async store(name, text) {
            const directory = location(this);
            filename(name);
            if (typeof text !== "string") throw new Error("Expected file text");
            const handle = await directory.getFileHandle(name, {create: true});
            const stream = await handle.createWritable();
            try {
                await stream.write(text);
                await stream.close();
            } catch (error) {
                try { await stream.abort(); } catch {}
                throw error;
            }
        },
        async remove(name) {
            const directory = location(this);
            filename(name);
            await directory.getFileHandle(name);
            await directory.removeEntry(name);
        },
        async list_files(signal) {
            const directory = location(this);
            signal?.throwIfAborted();
            const names = [];
            for await (const [name, handle] of directory.entries()) {
                signal?.throwIfAborted();
                if (handle.kind === "file") names.push(name);
            }
            signal?.throwIfAborted();
            return names.sort();
        }
    };

]]></code></section>
</template>
